  "scope": "The actual 256-slot minimum-positive controller constructs its positive-cost inventory from original numerator bits, then passes the literal returned record list to the existing stable rational argmin. Both real child calls and the returned retained record share one append-only physical heap. A stored-word/score relation is preserved by the actual first-tie selector and refines exactly BinaryFractionalDispatch.minimumPositive, including empty/all-zero inputs and padded fields. The same-run paid bound depends only on original row bit/list sizes; every field-width certificate is derived from those original bits. Twelve physical cases inspect original rational/index pointers, first equal-fraction ties, later minima, duplicate words and preserved inputs/source/stack. The old operation counter is not identified. Initial storage and physical-state bounds, guess construction and the full solver join remain explicit.",
  "pending": [
    "independent semantic review",
    "combined production integration and exact CI"
  ]
}
